{
  "name": "Schedule social posts from a Google Sheet with FoPost",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Schedule social posts from a Google Sheet\n\n### How it works\nPlan posts in a spreadsheet and let FoPost publish them. Each new row with text and a future **Publish At** time becomes a scheduled post on the accounts you pick, with the photo from **Image URL** when there is one. Rows without text or with a past time are skipped.\n\nMade for teams that plan content in a shared sheet: a real estate office adding new listings, a car dealer adding new arrivals, or a salon sharing its latest work.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the **FoPost** community node: Settings → Community Nodes → Install → `@fopost/n8n-nodes-fopost` (tested with 0.2.0). Docs: https://github.com/fopost/fopost-n8n\n2. Create a FoPost API key at fopost.com → Settings → API Keys and add it as a **FoPost API** credential.\n3. Create a sheet with the columns `Text`, `Image URL` and `Publish At` (format `2026-12-01 09:30`). Example row: `Just listed: 3-bed townhouse on Maple Street, open house Saturday` · `https://yourbrand.com/photos/maple.jpg` · `2026-12-05 10:00`.\n4. Add a **Google Sheets Trigger** credential and pick the sheet in **New row in content sheet**.\n5. Open **Configure** and set your FoPost workspace ID, the account IDs (comma-separated) and the time zone your sheet uses.\n\n### Customization\nAdd an `Accounts` column and use it instead of the fixed list in **Configure**.\n\n### Limitations\nOnly rows added after activation are picked up; edits to a row do not change its post.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 520
      },
      "id": "2b9f2d24-e63b-5a60-b393-72f3910923ba",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -260
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read new rows\nRows need text and a valid time in the future.",
